# Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com> (2026-09-25)
# KDE Plasma 6.8 beta 2 (6.7.91), opt-in only. Plasma numbers the next
# series' betas x.y.90 / x.y.91, so every atom below is a pre-release of 6.8.
# The ebuilds come from the Gentoo KDE team's overlay (github.com/gentoo/kde,
# 97636d8), which masks the same set as UNRELEASED. bentoo changes nothing
# but the # BENTOO-DIVERGENCE: comment tags that gentoo-parity.sh reads.
#
# The family is all-or-nothing. Each ebuild asks for its siblings at
# >=${KDE_CATV}, i.e. >=6.7.91, so unmasking one package without the rest
# leaves an atom nothing satisfies -- the failure that broke spectacle in
# e2695dfeb. To opt in, copy the atoms below verbatim into
# /etc/portage/package.unmask/plasma-6.8-beta (a stable-keyword system also
# needs them in package.accept_keywords).
#
# kwin-x11, kgamma, wacomtablet and plasma-login-sessions have no 6.7.91: the
# 6.8 series drops them, and ::gentoo still carries their 6.7.x. The last one
# is a hard block (plasma-login-manager-6.7.91 has !kde-plasma/plasma-login-
# sessions), so remove it first; the other three stay on 6.7.x built against
# 6.8 libraries, which upstream no longer tests.
#
# The atoms are deliberately unqualified: Portage stamps them "::bentoo", which
# is where these ebuilds live, and ::gentoo has no 6.7.91 to mask.
#
# Remove this block together with every 6.7.91 ebuild once ::gentoo ships
# 6.8.0. From then on a copy here is REDUNDANT (gentoo-parity.sh says so), and
# 6.8.0 already outranks 6.7.91 for everyone who unmasked it.
~app-backup/kup-6.7.91
~kde-plasma/aurorae-6.7.91
~kde-plasma/bluedevil-6.7.91
~kde-plasma/breeze-6.7.91
~kde-plasma/breeze-grub-6.7.91
